Chapter: CanopenEncodeTest

  cites Encode chapter Canopen

 Exercise CANopen: COB-ID composition, NMT command, heartbeat, and an
 expedited SDO download frame. Byte and identifier values checked
 against the CiA 301 layout. opening returns the count of passing checks.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

Section: Checks

 Node 5: TPDO1 COB-ID 0x185, SDO receive 0x605, heartbeat 0x705.

  check-tpdo1 : Integer
  check-tpdo1 =
   flag (co-cob-id co-fc-tpdo1 5 == #185)

  check-sdo-cob : Integer
  check-sdo-cob =
   flag (if co-cob-id co-fc-sdo-rx 5 == #605 then co-cob-id co-fc-heartbeat 5 == #705 else False)

  check-nmt : Integer
  check-nmt =
   flag (bytes-eq (co-nmt-command co-nmt-start 5) [1, 5])

  check-sdo-download : Integer
  check-sdo-download =
   flag (bytes-eq (co-sdo-download-expedited #6040 0 [15, 0]) [43, 64, 96, 0, 15, 0, 0, 0])

  opening : Integer =
   let a = check-tpdo1
   in let b = check-sdo-cob
   in let c = check-nmt
   in let d = check-sdo-download
   in a + b + c + d
